#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:118
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Inföhren"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:125
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&dolphin; is a file manager for &kde; which aims to improve usability at the "
"user interface level. &dolphin; is not intended to be a competitor to "
"&konqueror;. &dolphin; focuses only on being a file manager whereas "
"&konqueror; is a universal viewer of many file types. This development "
"approach allows for concentrating on optimizing the user interface for the "
"specific task of file management."
msgstr ""
"&dolphin; is en Dateipleger för &kde;, de de Bruukborkeit över de Böversiet "
"verbetern will. &dolphin; schall keen Konkurangs to &konqueror; wesen. "
"&dolphin; schall bloots en Dateipleger wesen, bides &konqueror; en "
"Universaalkieker för vele Dateitypen is. Dit Vörgahn bi't Utwickeln maakt "
"dat mööglich, wi maakt toeerst de Böversiet beter för de Opgaven, de bi't "
"Plegen vun Dateien so anfallt."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:133
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Please report any problems or feature requests to the &dolphin; author via "
"the bug report dialog. This is accessible from the "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Help</guimenu><guimenuitem>Report Bug...</guimenuitem></"
"menuchoice> menu of the application."
msgstr ""
"Maak bitte &dolphin; sien Schriever all Problemen un fehlen Funkschonen över "
"den Fehlerbericht-Dialoog künnig. Den kannst Du över dat Programm sien Menü "
"mit <menuchoice><guimenu>Hülp</guimenu><guimenuitem>Fehler künnig maken...</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice> opropen."

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:142
#, no-c-format
msgid "&dolphin; Interface"
msgstr "&dolphin;-Böversiet"

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:159
#, no-c-format
msgid "&dolphin; Features"
msgstr "&dolphin;-Funkschonen"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:160
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&dolphin; does not represent a wild departure from the &konqueror; file "
"manager interface. There are certain paradigms in use however, which may "
"require some readjustment on the user's part. An attempt is made below to "
"explain these in an effort to provide a more enjoyable experience for our "
"users."
msgstr ""
"&dolphin; steiht nich för en wild Afrücken vun &konqueror; sien Dateipleeg-"
"Böversiet. Man dat gifft en poor Prinzipien, de sik en Bruker villicht "
"eerstmaal anwarrn mutt. Nerrn, dat is de Versöök, disse to verkloren, so dat "
"för uns Brukers dor en beter Beleefnis bi rutkummt."

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:165
#, no-c-format
msgid "&dolphin; User Interface"
msgstr "&dolphin;-Brukerkoppelsteed"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:167
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The default &dolphin; interface consists of a (1) menu bar, (2) toolbar, (3) "
"location bar, (4) workspace, (6) Places Panel, (7) Information Panel and (8) "
"status bar."
msgstr ""
"&dolphin; sien Standard-Koppelsteed besteiht ut (1) den Menübalken, (2) den "
"Warktüüchbalken, (3) den Steedbalken, (4) dat Arbeitrebeet, (5) dat "
"Stedenpaneel, (7) dat Infopaneel un (8) den Statusbalken."

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:174 index.docbook:240 index.docbook:264 index.docbook:290
#: index.docbook:375 index.docbook:397 index.docbook:415 index.docbook:433
#: index.docbook:459 index.docbook:493 index.docbook:511
#, no-c-format
msgid "Here's a screenshot of &dolphin;"
msgstr "So süht &dolphin; ut"

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:180
#, no-c-format
msgid "&dolphin; Screenshot"
msgstr "&dolphin;-Schirmfoto"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:186
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The location bar displays the path to the current folder. The location bar "
"has two versions. By default location is chosen through the 'bread crumb' "
"display. The bread crumb display makes each folder a link which can be used "
"to immediately go to the entry. The <filename class=\"directory\">/home/"
"peter/Documents</filename> entry in the bread crumb view would become 'Home "
"> peter > Documents' with Home, peter, and Documents being clickable links "
"which are able go to there respective locations. This makes navigation to "
"folders above the current folder easier and more intuitive. There is also "
"the classic \"location view\" which is a text box in which you can type the "
"full path of the folder you wish to view."
msgstr ""
"De Steedbalken wiest den Padd na den aktuellen Orner. Dat gifft dor twee "
"Verschonen vun. Standardwies warrt de Steed mit de »Brootkrömenspoor« "
"utsöcht. Binnen de Krömenspoor is elkeen Orner en Link, över den Een "
"direktemang na den Orner hengahn kann. De Orner <filename class=\"directory"
"\">/home/peter/Documents</filename> warrt dor binnen as »Home > peter > "
"Documents« wiest. »Home«, »peter« un »Documents« laat sik anklicken, de Links "
"föhrt na de angeven Steden. Sodennig warrt dat veel eenfacher, wenn Een na "
"en överornt Orner will. Dat gifft ok dat klass'sche »Steedfeld«, also dat "
"Textfeld, na dat Du den helen Padd vun den Orner, na den Du henwullt, "
"ingeven kannst."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:190
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To switch from breadcrumbs to location view, simply click to the right of "
"the breadcrumb area. To change back, click the newly appeared yellow arrow "
"to the right of the location bar."
msgstr ""
"Wullt Du vun de Brootkrömels na't Steedfeld wesseln, klick eenfach "
"rechterhand dat Brootkrömenrebeet. Wullt Du torüchwesseln, klick op den nieg "
"opdukten gelen Piel rechts dat Steedfeld."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:191
#, no-c-format
msgid "To change the default &dolphin; view, please see the settings section."
msgstr ""
"Wullt Du &dolphin; sien Standardansicht wesseln, kiek binnen den Afnsitt "
"»Instellen«."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:198
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The workspace shows the contents of the current folder. The workspace can "
"also be set to \"Split\" mode and show two folders simultaneously."
msgstr ""
"Dat Arbeitrebeet wiest den Inholt vun den aktuellen Orner. Dat Arbeitrebeet "
"lett sik ok op »Deelt« Bedrief setten un wiest denn twee Ornern op eenmaal."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:202
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The status bar shows a limited amount of data relating to the file hovered "
"over and the current folder. When a file is hovered over, the status bar "
"shows the file name, the filesize and the file type &eg; JPEG. When no file "
"has been highlighted or hovered over, the status bar shows the amount of "
"files and folders in the current folder. At all times the status bar shows "
"the amount of storage space that has currently been used on the current "
"mount point, as well as the maximum space available on the mount point &eg; "
"<filename class=\"directory\">/home/</filename>."
msgstr ""
"De Statusbalken wiest wat Informatschonen över de Datei, op de Du jüst "
"wiest, un över den aktuellen Orner. Wiest Du op en Datei, wiest de "
"Statusbalken ehr Dateinaam, de Dateigrött un den Dateityp, &eg; JPEG. Is "
"keen Datei rutheevt oder wiest Du op keen, wiest de Balken de Tall vun "
"Dateien un Ornern binnen den aktuellen Orner. To all Tieden wiest de "
"Statusbalken den Spiekerruum, de opstunns op de aktuelle Inhangsteed al "
"bruukt is, blang den tohööchst verföögboren Ruum op de Inhangsteed, &eg; "
"<filename class=\"directory\">/home/</filename>."

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:208
#, no-c-format
msgid "&dolphin; Workspace"
msgstr "&dolphin;-Arbeitrebeet"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:210
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The &dolphin; workspace can display the contents of a folder in a variety of "
"views. There are three viewing modes Icons, Details, and Columns. Each of "
"these can have Preview enabled. This changes the icons into showing a "
"preview of the file, rather than an simply icon."
msgstr ""
"Du kannst en Orner sien Inholt mit en Reeg Ansichten wiesen. Dat gifft dree "
"Ansichten: Lüttbiller, Enkelheiten un Striepen. För all dree lett sik de "
"Vöransicht-Funkschoon bruken, mit de ansteed de Lüttbiller Vöransichten vun "
"de Dateien wiest warrt."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:213
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guibutton>Icons</guibutton> view shows the contents of the folder via "
"the file icon type &eg; an <acronym>MP3</acronym> file will be represented "
"with the icon for an <acronym>MP3</acronym> file. Sub-folders are "
"represented in the form of a folder icon. The folder icon is defined by the "
"&kde; icon theme currently in use, however individual folders can have their "
"icon changed manually if the user wishes. This can be done via the "
"properties dialog."
msgstr ""
"De <guibutton>Lüttbiller</guibutton>-Ansicht wiest den Inholt vun den Orner "
"över de Dateityp-Lüttbiller; &eg; warrt en <acronym>MP3</acronym>-Datei mit "
"dat Lüttbild för <acronym>MP3</acronym>-Dateien dorstellt. Ünnerornern warrt "
"mit en Orner-Lüttbild wiest. Dat Orner-Lüttbild warrt mit &kde; sien "
"Lüttbildmuster fastleggt, dat jüst in Bruuk is, man Du kannst de Ornern "
"binnen den Egenschappen-Dialoog ok vun Hand en egen Lüttbild towiesen."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:218
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guibutton>Details</guibutton> view lists the contents of a folder "
"whilst also displaying additional properties about the file. The default "
"&dolphin; configuration only displays the size of the file and the date it "
"was last modified. The choice of additional information shown can be changed "
"by right clicking on the column header and selecting the information you "
"wish to view or in <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</"
"guimenu><guisubmenu>Configure &dolphin;...</guisubmenu></menuchoice>"
msgstr ""
"De <guibutton>Enkelheiten</guibutton>-Ansicht wiest mehr Egenschappen vun de "
"Dateien. Mit &dolphin; sien Standardinstellen warrt bloots de Dateigrött un "
"dat Datum vun de verleden Ännern wiest. De Köör vun Informatschonen, de bito "
"wiest warrt, lett sik topassen, wenn Du op den Striepenkopp rechtsklickst un "
"de Feller utsöchst, de Du wiesen wullt, oder ok över "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Instellen</guimenu><guisubmenu>&dolphin; instellen...</"
"guisubmenu></menuchoice>"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:222
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guibutton>Columns</guibutton> view allows multiple levels of the folder "
"structure to be viewed at once. Each time a folder is clicked a new pane "
"appears to the right of the current listing showing the contents of that "
"folder."
msgstr ""
"Mit de <guibutton>Streipen</guibutton>-Ansicht laat sik verscheden Evenen "
"vun den Ornerboom op eenmaal bekieken. Jümmers, wenn Du op en Orner klickst, "
"dukt rechts dor vun en nieg Paneel mit den Orner sien Inholt op."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:227
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guibutton>Preview</guibutton> view is similar to the icons view. The "
"difference is that wherever possible previews of the files are shown. This "
"function works for a number of image types including; JPG, PNG, XCF, "
"<acronym>SVG</acronym> and numerous others. The previews view is also "
"capable of showing the first 14 lines from text documents. &dolphin; is also "
"capable of displaying a preview of &HTML; and <acronym>PDF</acronym> files "
"in the previews view. It is also possible to modify the size of the previews "
"via the Configure &dolphin; dialog."
msgstr ""
"De <guibutton>Vöransicht</guibutton>-Ansicht is liek to de Lüttbiller-"
"Ansicht. De Verscheel is, jümmers wenn mööglich, warrt Vöransichten vun de "
"Dateien wiest. Dat funkscheneert för en Reeg Bildtypen, so as JPG, PNG, XCF, "
"<acronym>SVG</acronym> un anner Typen. Mit den Vöransichten-Bedrief laat sik "
"ok de eersten 14 Regen ut Textdokmenten ankieken, un &dolphin; kann ok "
"Vöransichten för &HTML;- un <acronym>PDF</acronym>-Dateien wiesen. Binnen "
"&dolphin; sien Instellen kannst Du ok de Vöransichten ehr Grött topassen."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:232
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Changing the view of the folder a user is working in is as simple as "
"clicking the icon of the view they wish to use. This will cause the "
"workspace view to change accordingly."
msgstr ""
"Will en Bruker de Ansicht vun den Orner wesseln, binnen den he jüst togang "
"is, bruukt he bloots op de Ansicht ehr Lüttbild klicken, denn warrt dat "
"Arbeitrebeet de Köör topasst."

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:246
#, no-c-format
msgid "&dolphin; Workspace View Buttons"
msgstr "&dolphin; sien Arbeitrebeet-Ansichtknööp"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:252
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The workspace in &dolphin; is capable of showing two folders within the same "
"window, known as split workspaces. In order to enable or disable the split "
"workspace mode toggle the icon on the taskbar. Another way to enable or "
"disable the split workspace mode is to use the <menuchoice><guimenu>View</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Split</guimenuitem></menuchoice> menu option."
msgstr ""
"Dat Arbeitrebeet vun &dolphin; kann twee Ornern binnen een Finster wiesen, "
"wat as »Deelt Arbeitrebeet« begäng is. Mit dat Lüttbild op den "
"Warktüüchbalken kannst de deelte Bedriefoort an- un utmaken, oder du bruukst "
"den Menüindrag <menuchoice><guimenu>Ansicht</guimenu><guimenuitem>Deelt</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice>."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:256
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this option is enabled then the workspace will split apart. Two separate "
"workspace areas will be available for use, along with two separate location "
"bars. Clicking on either workspace will make it the active workspace. If the "
"user toggles the split workspace mode off, then the currently active "
"workspace will remain, while the inactive workspace will close."
msgstr ""
"Warrt disse Optschoon anmaakt, deelt sik dat Arbeitrebeet. Nu gifft dat twee "
"Arbeitrebeden un twee Steedbalkens. Klickst Du op een vun de Arbeitrebeden, "
"maakst Du dat dor mit an. Maakst Du den deelten Bedrief ut, warrt dat aktive "
"Arbeitrebeet övernahmen un dat annere tomaakt."

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:270
#, no-c-format
msgid "&dolphin; In Split Workspace Mode"
msgstr "&dolphin; mit deelt Arbeitrebeet"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:276
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&dolphin; is capable of remembering the workspace view on a per-folder "
"basis. For example, if while viewing <filename class=\"directory\">/home/"
"peter/Pictures/</filename> the user choses to use the preview view, then the "
"next time the user enters that folder, the view will be changed to the "
"preview view. This is especially useful for folders containing mainly "
"images. The feature only works for local folders which the user has read/"
"write permissions to. &dolphin; will also remember the viewing mode it was "
"in when last running &eg; single workspace or split workspace."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:280
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&dolphin; can also display files and sub-folders that are hidden in the "
"current folder &eg; files such as <filename>.dolphin</filename> and sub-"
"folder such as <filename class=\"directory\">.kde/</filename>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:284
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Hidden files and sub-folders can be distinguished from non-hidden file and "
"sub-folders by their colouring. Hidden files/sub-folders are fainter than "
"non-hidden files/sub-folders."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:296
#, no-c-format
msgid "&dolphin; Showing Hidden Files/Sub-folders Enabled"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:302
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To enable the showing of hidden files and sub-folders you can select "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>View</guimenu><guimenuitem>Show Hidden Files</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:306
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&dolphin; is able to sort the contents of a folder in a number of ways. "
"These are; By Name, By Date, By Size and Descending order. These only apply "
"to the current folder the user is currently in and do not affect other "
"folders. As with the Views Modes the Sorting order is saved for this folder."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:310
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To change the way the folder is sorted, via the menu "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>View</guimenu><guisubmenu>Sort By</guisubmenu></"
"menuchoice> (&eg; By Date)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:316
#, no-c-format
msgid "&dolphin; Panels"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:317
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&dolphin; allows a number of Panels to be placed in the workspace. These can "
"be enabled in <menuchoice><guimenu>View</guimenu><guisubmenu>Panels</"
"guisubmenu></menuchoice>. Those chosen can then be dragged around the "
"&dolphin; window by clicking and dragging the panel title. The panels "
"available are described below."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:321
#, no-c-format
msgid "Places"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:322
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Places</guilabel> panel is found at the left of the window by "
"default, The <guilabel>Places</guilabel> panel shows any locations you have "
"bookmarked. It also shows any disk or media attached to the computer. This "
"list corresponds with the list of places in the breadcrumbs menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:329
#, no-c-format
msgid "Information"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:330
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Information</guilabel> panel shows extended information about "
"the selected file(s), including size, type, and date of last modification. "
"Information also features a large preview of the selected file."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:336
#, no-c-format
msgid "Folders"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:337
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Folders</guilabel> panel shows a tree view structure of the "
"file system. It only shows folders. By selecting a folder the main &dolphin; "
"area changes to show the contents of the selected folder."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:343
#, no-c-format
msgid "Terminal"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:344
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This panel opens a terminal inside the &dolphin; workspace. The terminal "
"will open at the folder currently shown in the &dolphin; view. Changing "
"folder in the main &dolphin; view will change the working folder of the "
"terminal to match. Note: Changing folder in the terminal will not affect the "
"&dolphin; view. The terminal only works with local media."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:360
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using &dolphin;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:363
#, no-c-format
msgid "&dolphin; Navigation"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:365
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The main feature of &dolphin; that allows navigation of the file system is "
"the work space. Clicking on a sub-folder within the current folder changes "
"to this folder. Clicking on files within the workspace will open the file in "
"the default application for that file type."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:369
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The toolbar is also used for navigating the file system. The toolbar "
"contains two buttons essential for navigating the file system quickly and "
"easily, these are; <guiicon>Back</guiicon> and <guiicon>Forward</guiicon>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:381
#, no-c-format
msgid "&dolphin; Toolbar Buttons"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:387
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Other buttons can be added to the toolbar to further aid navigation or to "
"provide shortcuts for functions within &dolphin; &eg; deleting a file."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:391
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&dolphin; continually shows the folder that it is currently viewing the "
"contents of, via the location bar and the title bar. The location bar has "
"two views available. The first is the folder path view. This shows the path "
"to the current folder &eg; <filename class=\"directory\">/usr/share/apps/"
"dolphin/</filename>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:403
#, no-c-format
msgid "&dolphin; Displaying The Folder Path View"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:409
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The second view is the breadcrumb view. This allows the user to move to a "
"folder a number of folders back from the current one. This is achieved via a "
"tab like interface where the name of each previous folder is displayed and "
"can be clicked on to change into."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:421
#, no-c-format
msgid "&dolphin; Displaying The Breadcrumb View"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:427
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To switch from breadcrumbs to location view, simply click in the right part "
"of the breadcrumb area or use <menuchoice> <guimenu>View</guimenu> "
"<guisubmenu>Navigation Bar</guisubmenu> <guimenuitem>Edit Location</"
"guimenuitem> </menuchoice>. To change back, click the newly appeared yellow "
"arrow to the right of the location bar or use <menuchoice> <guimenu>View</"
"guimenu> <guisubmenu>Navigation Bar</guisubmenu> <guimenuitem>Show Full "
"Location</guimenuitem> </menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:439
#, no-c-format
msgid "&dolphin; Browse Button"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:445
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"With the folder path view the user is able to enter the whole path to the "
"folder they wish to enter. In order to do so, the user can toggle the browse "
"button to the folder path view or alternatively via the menu <menuchoice> "
"<guimenu>View</guimenu> <guisubmenu>Navigation Bar</guisubmenu> "
"<guimenuitem>Edit Location</guimenuitem> </menuchoice> then enter the path "
"to the folder they wish to enter. The user will notice as they are entering "
"the path, a box will open underneath the address bar showing the content of "
"the folder they are currently heading to. The content of this box will "
"change as they continue to enter the path to the folder, showing the folders "
"and the files beginning with the characters being entered &eg; <filename "
"class=\"directory\">/usr/share/apps/k</filename> would display everything "
"within the folder beginning with the k character."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:449
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If the breadcrumb view is enabled then the user is unable to enter the path "
"to the folder. The user must manually navigate the file system by clicking "
"the folders and sub-folders within the folders."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:453
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In order to aid the navigation of the file system, &dolphin; can use Places. "
"Places can be set for any location on the file system including virtual "
"folders such as \"trash:/\". Selecting a Place will display that folder or "
"virtual folder in the workspace."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:465
#, no-c-format
msgid "&dolphin; Bookmark Button Open"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:471
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In order to select a Place, the location bar must be set to the breadcrumb "
"view. Clicking the image of the home button (as set by the icon theme "
"currently in use) will drop down a list of all the available bookmarks. The "
"&dolphin; Places Panel also contains your Places list. This can be accessed "
"via switching the sidebar to bookmarks mode. The user then clicks the "
"desired Place to open that folder."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:481
#, no-c-format
msgid "&dolphin; Configuration"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:483
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In order to configure &dolphin; the user needs to access the &dolphin; "
"Configuration dialog. This can be accessed via the menu bar; <menuchoice> "
"<guimenu>Settings</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Configure &dolphin;...</"
"guimenuitem> </menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:487
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The &dolphin; Configuration dialog consists of three sections; "
"<guilabel>Startup</guilabel>, <guilabel>View Modes</guilabel>, and "
"<guilabel>General</guilabel>. Clicking one of these sections will make those "
"options available accordingly. The options available are displayed to the "
"right of the dialog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:499
#, no-c-format
msgid "&dolphin; Configuration Window Showing The General Options"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:505
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>General</guilabel> option allows users to set a number of "
"options for &dolphin;, these are; the default home location for the user "
"&eg; /home/Peter, the default view mode (all folders will use this view "
"unless they have already been changed) and wether or not split view is "
"enabled by default."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:517
#, no-c-format
msgid "&dolphin; Configuration Window Showing The View Options"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:523
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>View Modes</guilabel> option differs slightly from the "
"<guilabel>General</guilabel> option in that it has four tabs in the options. "
"The <guilabel>Icons</guilabel> tab allows users to set options to do with "
"the Icons View Mode &eg; icon size. The <guilabel>Details</guilabel> tab "
"allows users to set options relating to the Details View Mode &eg; what "
"information about files are shown. The Previews to allows users to set "
"options relating to the Previews View Mode &eg; the size of the preview "
"images."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:530
#, no-c-format
msgid "Quick Tips"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:532
#, no-c-format
msgid "The following are a number of tips to save time when using &dolphin;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:537
#, no-c-format
msgid "Quick Bookmarking"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:539
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To quickly create a bookmark of the folder currently being viewed, right "
"click in the work space and via the menu select \"Add to Places\". The "
"Bookmarking dialog will open, enter a name for the bookmark along with an "
"icon to represent the bookmark."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:546
#, no-c-format
msgid "Finding Files"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:548
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&dolphin; is capable of searching for files in a filesystem. If <keycombo "
"action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>F</keycap></keycombo> is pressed or using "
"<menuchoice> <guimenu>Tools</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Find File...</"
"guimenuitem> </menuchoice>, &kfind; will open already set up to search "
"within the current folder and any sub-folders contained within."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:555
#, no-c-format
msgid "Mounting Storage Media"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:557
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A quick way to mount Storage Media is to click on the device. This will "
"mount and open the device in &dolphin;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:563
#, no-c-format
msgid "Undo Actions"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:565
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&dolphin; is capable of undoing changes users have made to files. For "
"example if a user sent a file to the Trash, &dolphin; can undo this and move "
"it back to the folder it previously belonged in. To undo an action via the "
"menu <menuchoice> <guimenu>Edit</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Undo: (action name)</"
"guimenuitem> </menuchoice>, &eg; <guimenuitem>Undo: Rename</guimenuitem> or "
"by pressing <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>Z</keycap></keycombo>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:571
#, no-c-format
msgid "Renaming A Batch Of Files"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:573
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&dolphin; is capable of renaming a number of files at the same time. Each "
"file will have the file name specified, followed by a number for how many "
"files that have been chosen to rename &eg; Tester 1.png, Tester 2.png, "
"Tester 3.png. This is useful for when you have a number of audio files where "
"you wish to number them via their track number, or for photographs taken "
"from a digital camera."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:577
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If a user wishes to rename a batch of files they must first select the files "
"to be renamed. This can be done via dragging the mouse over the files to be "
"renamed, or via holding &Ctrl; and clicking each file to be renamed. The "
"user must then open the batch-rename dialog, this, can be done via pressing "
"<keycap>F2</keycap> or via the File menu; <menuchoice> <guimenu>File</"
"guimenu> <guimenuitem>Rename...</guimenuitem> </menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:581
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The user must then enter the name they wish to give the files. The # "
"character must also be present within the name (failure to include the # key "
"will result in an error as this indicates where the file number should be "
"sequentially increased for each file.) The files will then be renamed with a "
"number present within the file name."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:587
#, no-c-format
msgid "Comparing A Selection Of Files"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:589
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&dolphin; is capable of comparing a selection of files to see the "
"differences between them. For a user to be able to compare files then the "
"&kompare; application must be installed. &dolphin; can only compare the "
"files that &kompare; is capable on analyzing."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:593
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If a user wishes to compare a selection of files, then first they must "
"select the files to be compared. Then launch the &kompare; application via "
"the Tools menu; <menuchoice> <guimenu>Tools</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Compare "
"Files</guimenuitem> </menuchoice>. &kompare; will then open showing the "
"differences between the files."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:599
#, no-c-format
msgid "Filter A Selection Of Files"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:601
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&dolphin; is capable of filtering a selection of files within the workspace "
"via a text string. For example if a user wish to filter all of the "
"<acronym>MP3</acronym> files within a folder, they could filter for .mp3. "
"This would then filter out all of the files that did not have .mp3 within "
"their file name."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:605
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If a user wishes to filter a selection of files this can be done via the "
"filter bar. The user then enters the text they wish to filter for within "
"that folder. To enable the filter bar the user must press either the "
"<keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>I</keycap></keycombo> key or via "
"the Menu Bar; <menuchoice> <guimenu>Tools</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Show Filter "
"Bar</guimenuitem> </menuchoice>. To disable the filter bar the user must "
"press either the &Esc; key, or via the <menuchoice> <guimenu>Tools</guimenu> "
"<guimenuitem>Show Filter Bar</guimenuitem> </menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:615
#, no-c-format
msgid "Command Reference"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:624
#, no-c-format
msgid "The main &dolphin; window"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:627
#, no-c-format
msgid "The File Menu"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:632
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>File</guimenu> <guisubmenu>Create New</guisubmenu>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: index.docbook:636
#, no-c-format
msgid "Creates a new object in the current folder."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:640
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>N</keycap></keycombo> </"
"shortcut> <guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>New Window</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: index.docbook:647
#, no-c-format
msgid "Opens a new window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:651
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;&Shift;<keycap>N</keycap></"
"keycombo> </shortcut> <guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>New Tab</"
"guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: index.docbook:658
#, no-c-format
msgid "Opens a new tab."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:662
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\"><keycap>F2</keycap></keycombo> </"
"shortcut> <guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Rename</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: index.docbook:669
#, no-c-format
msgid "Renames the currently selected document(s)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:673
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\"><keycap>Del</keycap></keycombo> </"
"shortcut> <guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Move to Trash</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: index.docbook:680
#, no-c-format
msgid "Moves the currently selected file(s) to the trash."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:685
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Shift;<keycap>Del</keycap></keycombo> "
"</shortcut> <guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Delete</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: index.docbook:692
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Permanently deletes the currently selected file(s). The files are not moved "
"to the trash."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:696
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Alt;<keycap>Return</keycap></"
"keycombo> </shortcut> <guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Properties</"
"guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: index.docbook:703
#, no-c-format
msgid "Shows the properties dialog for the currently selected file(s)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:707
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>Q</keycap></keycombo> </"
"shortcut> <guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Quit</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: index.docbook:714
#, no-c-format
msgid "Exits &dolphin;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:722
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Edit Menu"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:727
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>Z</keycap></keycombo> </"
"shortcut> <guimenu>Edit</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Undo</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: index.docbook:734
#, no-c-format
msgid "Undoes the last action performed by &dolphin;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:738
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>X</keycap></keycombo> </"
"shortcut> <guimenu>Edit</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Cut</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: index.docbook:745
#, no-c-format
msgid "Cuts the currently selected file(s)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:749
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>C</keycap></keycombo> </"
"shortcut> <guimenu>Edit</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Copy</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: index.docbook:756
#, no-c-format
msgid "Copies the currently selected file(s)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:760
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>V</keycap></keycombo> </"
"shortcut> <guimenu>Edit</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Paste</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: index.docbook:767
#, no-c-format
msgid "Pastes the currently copied/cut files to the current folder."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:771
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>A</keycap></keycombo> </"
"shortcut> <guimenu>Edit</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Select All</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: index.docbook:778
#, no-c-format
msgid "Selects all files and folders in the current folder."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:782
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;&Shift;<keycap>A</keycap></"
"keycombo> </shortcut> <guimenu>Edit</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Invert Selection</"
"guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: index.docbook:789
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Selects all unselected items and deselects all selected items in the current "
"folder."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:798
#, no-c-format
msgid "The View Menu"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:803
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>+</keycap></keycombo> </"
"shortcut> <guimenu>View</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Zoom In</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: index.docbook:810
#, no-c-format
msgid "Increases the size of icons in the workspace."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:814
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>-</keycap></keycombo> </"
"shortcut> <guimenu>View</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Zoom Out</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: index.docbook:821
#, no-c-format
msgid "Decreases the size of icons in the workspace."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:825
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>View</guimenu> <guisubmenu>View Mode...</guisubmenu>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: index.docbook:829
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Changes the workspace view to show <guimenuitem>Icons</guimenuitem> "
"(<keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>1</keycap></keycombo>), "
"<guimenuitem>Details</guimenuitem> (<keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;"
"<keycap>2</keycap></keycombo>) or <guimenuitem>Columns</guimenuitem> "
"(<keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>3</keycap></keycombo>)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:833
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>View</guimenu> <guisubmenu>Sort By</guisubmenu>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: index.docbook:837
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Changes whether items are sorted by <guimenuitem>Name</guimenuitem>, "
"<guimenuitem>Size</guimenuitem>, <guimenuitem>Date</guimenuitem>, "
"<guimenuitem>Permissions</guimenuitem>, <guimenuitem>Owner</guimenuitem>, "
"<guimenuitem>Group</guimenuitem> or <guimenuitem>Type</guimenuitem>. "
"<guimenuitem>Descending</guimenuitem> reverses the sort order."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:841
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>View</guimenu> <guisubmenu>Additional Information</guisubmenu>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:845
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Displays additional information</action> like <guimenuitem>Size</"
"guimenuitem>, <guimenuitem>Date</guimenuitem>, <guimenuitem>Permissions</"
"guimenuitem>, <guimenuitem>Owner</guimenuitem>, <guimenuitem>Group</"
"guimenuitem> or <guimenuitem>Type</guimenuitem> in the different views."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:849
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>View</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Preview</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:853
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Displays a symbolic preview of the file contents </action> in the "
"different view modes."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:857
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>View</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Show in Groups</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:861
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Displays</action> the content of the current folder grouped by file "
"type."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:865
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Alt;<keycap>.</keycap></keycombo> </"
"shortcut> <guimenu>View</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Show Hidden Files</"
"guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: index.docbook:872
#, no-c-format
msgid "Shows all the hidden files and sub-folders within the current folder."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:876
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\"><keycap>F3</keycap></keycombo> </"
"shortcut> <guimenu>View</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Split</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: index.docbook:883
#, no-c-format
msgid "Enables and disables the split view workspace mode."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:887
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\"><keycap>F5</keycap></keycombo> </"
"shortcut> <guimenu>View</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Reload</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: index.docbook:894
#, no-c-format
msgid "Reloads the current folder."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:898
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>View</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Stop</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: index.docbook:902
#, no-c-format
msgid "Stops loading/reading the contents of the current folder."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:906
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>View</guimenu> <guisubmenu>Panels</guisubmenu>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:910
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Enables and disables</action> the different panels, &eg; "
"<guimenuitem>Places</guimenuitem> (<keycap>F9</keycap>), "
"<guimenuitem>Information</guimenuitem> (<keycap>F11</keycap>), "
"<guimenuitem>Folders</guimenuitem> (<keycap>F7</keycap>) and "
"<guimenuitem>Terminal</guimenuitem> (<keycap>F4</keycap>)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:914
