#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1097
#, no-c-format
msgid "Frequently asked Questions"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1112
#, no-c-format
msgid "How do I add my own custom service menus to &dolphin;?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1115
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&dolphin; can use the majority of service menus created for &konqueror;, "
"however &dolphin; does impose one limitation on the service menus: Service "
"menu entries that add themselves to the top level of the context menu will "
"automatically be placed below the Actions sub-menu. This prevents that the "
"context menu will get crowded."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1119
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To add a custom service menu to &dolphin; save the service menu to the "
"&dolphin; service menu folder, this can be found in /home/house/.kde/share/"
"apps/dolphin/servicemenus/. If the servicemenus sub-folder does not exist in "
"the &dolphin; folder, then create the sub-folder and save the service menu "
"to that folder. The next time the user launch &dolphin; the service menu "
"will be available."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1127
#, no-c-format
msgid "How do I make &dolphin; my default file manager?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1130
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To make &dolphin; the default file manager for &kde; from the &kde; control "
"center open the File Associations section via; &kde; Components>File "
"Associations. If the user adds &dolphin; to the list of applications for the "
"folder mime type and make it the first choice, then &dolphin; will become "
"the default application to open any folder with. The folder mime type can be "
"found by expanding the inode section of Known Types."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1134
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To make &dolphin; the default file manager for the virtual folders created "
"by &kde; &eg; system:/ then again in the File Associations section of the "
"control center expand the inode section of Known Types. Under the "
"system_directory mime type, add &dolphin; to the list of applications, "
"however instead of choosing &dolphin; from the kmenu, type the following in "
"to the text box at the top; dolphin %u. The virtual folders created by &kde; "
"will then be opened by &dolphin; as default."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1145
#, no-c-format
msgid "Miscellaneous Questions"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1150
#, no-c-format
msgid "Does &dolphin; intended to replace &konqueror;?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1153
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&dolphin; is not intended to be a competitor to &konqueror;: &konqueror; "
"acts as universal viewer being able to show &HTML; pages, text documents, "
"folders and a lot more, whereas &dolphin; focuses on being only a file "
"manager. This approach allows to optimize the user interface for the task of "
"file management."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1161
#, no-c-format
msgid "How can I get involved with the development of &dolphin;?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1164
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The easiest way to get involved with &dolphin; is to drop the developers an "
"email. If you email Peter Penz (Lead Developer/Project Leader), what you can "
"do, how much time you can devote &etc; and he will let you know what you can "
"do in the project. If you wish to contribute to the documentation email "
"Michael Austin (Documentation Leader). He can then fill you in on the "
"situation &eg; what needs to be added/finished, the procedure for submitting "
"documentation."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1167
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The email addresses of Peter Penz and Michael Austin can be found on the "
"main page of the documentation, or in the Credits section."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1175
#, no-c-format
msgid "Where do I submit bug reports to?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1178
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Bug reports should only be submitted for released versions of &dolphin;, "
"please do not submit bug reports for the Subversion release of &dolphin; as "
"this is expected to break due to its constant development."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1181
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The official channel for submitting bug reports is via the &kde; bug "
"tracking system. Alternatively bug reports can be emailed to Peter Penz "
"(email address is found on the main page or the credits section)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1184
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The &kde; bug tracker can be found at <ulink url=\"http://bugs.kde.org"
"\">http://bugs.kde.org</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1192
#, no-c-format
msgid "Where do I submit feature requests to?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1195
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The official channel for submitting feature requests is via the &kde; bug "
"tracking system. Alternatively feature requests can be emailed to Peter Penz "
"(email address is found on the main page or the credits section)."
msgstr ""

